t % float:** 17.56% | **DTC:** 8.63\n- **Fiscal basis:** FY ends late-December; \"FY2025\" = year ended 2025-12-26. TTM through 2026-03-27.\n\n---\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 1 \u2014 MACRO CONTEXT\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n**Step 1-1 \u2014 Macro variable check**  \n- **10Y Treasury:** ~4.71% (Trading Economics / CNBC, 2026-08-21) [Actual] \u2014 elevated, stable-to-rising.  \n- **Fed funds:** 3.50\u20133.75%, unchanged five consecutive meetings (Federal Reserve FOMC minutes, 2026-07-29; Trading Economics) [Actual]. Market prices ~1-in-3 chance of a *hike*. Policy stance: NEUTRAL-to-TIGHTENING.  \n- **DXY:** ~98.6\u201399.0 (Trading Economics, 2026-08-20) [Actual] \u2014 modestly weak dollar, mild tailwind for imported specialty food costs.  \n- **Inflation:** Net food inflation CHEF disclosed +4.9% in Q2 2026 (specialty +4.0%, center-of-plate +6.4%) [Actual] \u2014 elevated for the category.  \n- **Credit spreads:** Not retrieved in budget; proxy from S&P Global Ratings \u2014 CHEF margin expansion to 7.6% EBITDA margin in 2026, 7.8% in 2027 (S&P, retrieved 2026-08) [Estimate]. Spreads assumed average-to-tight.  \n- **Economic cycle:** Late expansion. Real consumer spending on discretionary restaurant occasions remains positive but cyclical risk rising.\n\n**Step 1-2 \u2014 Regime classification (probability distribution, sums to 100%)**  \n- Goldilocks (low rates + growth): 25%  \n- Reflation (high rates + growth): 35%  \n- Stagflation (high rates + low growth): 25%  \n- Recession (low rates + low growth): 15%  \n**Total = 100%.**\n\n**Step 1-3 \u2014 Sensitivity matrix**  \n| Axe | Score | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| Interest rate | \u22122 | Floating-rate ABL; consumer discretionary exposure; convert refi in 2028 |\n| Dollar | +1 | Weak dollar helps imported product costs; ~77%+ domestic revenue |\n| Liquidity | +1 | ABL availability; equity issuance possible but dilutive |\n| Economic cycle | +2 | Hotel/fine-dining/cruise end-market highly cyclical (2020 evidence) |\n| Commodity | \u22121 | Center-of-plate protein inflation 6.4% \u2014 margin risk |\n\n**Step 1-4 \u2014 Macro alignment judgment**  \nWeighted expected macro impact: **MILD HEADWIND** (cycle risk offset by weak-dollar tailwind). Conviction **\u22120.5 step**; accelerate split entry if buying. No change to IV.\n\n---\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 1.5 \u2014 BASE RATE & HISTORICAL PATTERN\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n**Step 1.5-1 \u2014 Base rates**  \n| Item | Base rate | CHEF-specific |\n|---|---|---|\n| 5-year survival, established $4B+ revenue distributor | ~90% | Survived COVID drawdown (\u221230% rev in 2020); strong |\n| Company with 3.5% op. margin reaching 5%+ in 5 years | ~30\u201340% | The entire bull case\u2014marginal at base rate |\n| Roll-up M&A achieving ROIC > WACC in food distribution | ~30\u201340% | CHEF has positive but modest track record (2023\u201325 improved) |\n| Revenue CAGR 7\u201310% for 5 years at this scale | ~25\u201335% | Partially acquisition-supported; also achieved 2020\u201325 (30.1% incl. M&A) |\n\n**Step 1.5-2 \u2014 Deviation from base rate**  \nMy base case gives management's 2030 plan a ~55% success probability (7\u20138% EBITDA margin). Justifications for deviation: (1) 3 consecutive years of raised guidance; (2) mix shift to higher-margin specialty/Center-of-the-Plate; (3) post-COVID scale in new distrib. capacity (TX, NV, NE). SUFFICIENT, but not overwhelming.\n\n**Step 1.5-3 \u2014 Base rate shock check**  \nMarket at 15x forward EBITDA implies full delivery of 2030 targets. That is **1.8\u20132.0\u00d7 the base rate**. Additional evidence required before paying this price \u2192 RED FLAG, reflected in Hold rating.\n\n---\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 2 \u2014 BUSINESS QUALITY\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n**Step 2-1 \u2014 Business understanding** (3 sentences)  \nCHEF distributes specialty and center-of-the-plate foods (artisanal cheese, truffles, custom-cut proteins, seafood) to independent restaurants, hotels, cruise ships, and caterers. The company acts as a curated intermediary bundling thousands of SKUs with culinary expertise and logistics. Its model depends on the vibrancy of the upscale independent restaurant/hospitality channel and its ability to differentiate service vs. broadline giants (Sysco, US Foods).  \nUnderstandability: **HIGH**.\n\n**Step 2-2 \u2014 Moat assessment**  \n| Moat type | Score (0\u20133) | Direction |\n|---|---|---|\n| Intangibles (brand/curation) | 2 | Stable |\n| Switching costs | 2 | Stable |\n| Network effects | 1 | Stable |\n| Cost advantage (scale) | 2 | Widening |\n| Economies of scale | 2 | Widening |\n| Regulatory barriers | 1 | Stable |\n| Data moat | 1 | Improving (AI rollout across sales/pricing/procurement) |\n| **Total** | **11/21** | **Narrow / Widening** |\n\n**Step 2-3 \u2014 Lynch classification**  \n**FAST GROWER with cyclicality.** Revenue CAGR 30.1% over last 5 FY (incl. M&A); organic growth consistently 8\u201312%. Cyclicality shown in 2020 (\u221230%) and COVID recovery. Lynch checkpoints \u2014 earnings growth double-digit over 3+ years: YES in recovery; BUT leverage/cyclicality adds caution.\n\n**Step 2-4 \u2014 Financial strength scorecard [Actual]**  \n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Revenue CAGR (5 yr) | 30.1% |\n| Operating margin (FY25) | 3.5% (median 3.3%) |\n| Gross margin (FY25) | 24.2% |\n| ROE (vendor) | 15.3% |\n| FCF (FY25) | $88M |\n| Net debt / adj. EBITDA (Q2'26 call) | 1.6\u00d7 |\n| Interest coverage (approx, EBIT/int) | ~6\u20137\u00d7 |\n\n**Judgment:** ADEQUATE-to-GOOD. Profitable and growing, but structurally low-margin, levered, and cyclical.\n\n**Step 2-5 \u2014 Capital allocation scorecard**  \n1. Buyback efficiency: 0 (no consistent buyback; share count +5.8% CAGR 3-yr).  \n2. M&A track record: 2 (accretive deals, some integration risk).  \n3. Capex efficiency: 2 (incremental ROIC > WACC, targeted at growth capacity).  \n4. Rationality of mix: 2 (reinvest vs. buybacks, ABL available).  \n5. Guidance accuracy: 3 (raised guidance in 2025 and 2026).  \nInsider: Founder-led (Pappas) but insider ownership ~10.5%; no large 6-month *net buys* retrieved [Unconfirmed].  \n**Score: 9/15 + 0 bonus = 9/15.**\n\n---\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u25