ling with revenue [Assumption]. Interest = estimated from 2028 convert $250M @2.375% + ABL + op-lease interest [Assumption \u2014 debt components partially unconfirmed]. Tax 27% [Assumption from historical effective rate].\n\n*Free cash flow bridge (FCFF):*\n| Year | EBITDA | \u2212 D&A | \u2212 Interest | \u2212 Tax | \u2212 Capex (~1% rev) | \u2212 \u0394WC (\u2248 1% rev) | **FCFF** |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026 | 310 | 120 | 32 | 43 | 45 | 45 | **25** |\n| 2027 | 355 | 130 | 35 | 51 | 49 | 49 | **41** |\n| 2028 | 400 | 140 | 40 | 59 | 53 | 53 | **55** |\n| 2029 | 450 | 150 | 38 | 71 | 58 | 58 | **75** |\n| 2030 | 485 | 160 | 34 | 79 | 63 | 63 | **86** |\n\n*(FCF conversion: 8%, 12%, 14%, 17%, 18% of EBITDA \u2014 meaningfully below 40\u201360% target because of lease-adjusted interest + \u0394WC; target not observable in reported FCF yet [Estimate].)*\n\n*WACC derivation [Assumption]:*  \n- Risk-free (10Y): 4.71% [Actual]  \n- Equity risk premium: 4.5% [Assumption]  \n- Beta: 1.0 [Assumption; vendor beta 1.391 is window-unstated \u2192 I use 1.0]  \n- Cost of equity: 4.71% + 1.0 \u00d7 4.5% = **9.2%**  \n- Cost of debt (pre-tax): ~5.5% [Assumption: 2.375% convert + ~6% ABL, blended] \u2192 after-tax 4.0%  \n- Weights: 20% debt / 80% equity (net debt $478M / EV $4.99B)  \n- **WACC = 0.8 \u00d7 9.2% + 0.2 \u00d7 4.0% \u2248 8.2%**  \n\n*Terminal:* g = **3.0%** (\u2248 long-run nominal GDP) [Assumption]. Terminal FCFF = 86 \u00d7 1.03 / (0.082 \u2212 0.03) = $1.70B.  \nPV of explicit FCFF (discounted at 8.2%):  \nPV26 = 25/1.082 = 23  \nPV27 = 41/1.1707 = 35  \nPV28 = 55/1.2664 = 43  \nPV29 = 75/1.3700 = 55  \nPV30 = 86/1.4819 = 58  \n\u03a3 PV explicit \u2248 **$214M**  \nPV terminal = 1.70B / 1.4819 \u2248 **$1.147B**  \n**Enterprise value \u2248 $1.36B**  \n+ Cash $121M \u2212 Net debt $478M = **Equity value \u2248 $1.00B**  \n\u00f7 Fully diluted shares \u2248 53.3M (46.0M basic + ~7.3M converts) \u2192 **IV \u2248 $18.8/share** \u2190 *clearly wrong.*\n\n**STOP \u2014 Model reconciliation error.**  \nThe assumed \u0394WC and capex are double-counting. Management-reported *net debt leverage* includes only $478M non-lease debt, and their FCF conversion target 40\u201360% produces FCF at the *adjusted EBITDA* line, *before* tax, not after. Fix: use **unlevered FCF from EBITDA toward firm** rather than after-tax-equity.\n\n*Corrected FCFF (unlevered):*  \nFCFF = EBITDA \u2212 D&A (tax shield ignored) \u2212 cash taxes on EBIT \u2212 capex \u2212 \u0394WC  \n| Year | EBITDA | D&A | EBIT | Taxes @27% | Capex | \u0394WC | **FCFF** |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026 | 310 | 120 | 190 | 51 | 45 | 35 | **179** |\n| 2027 | 355 | 130 | 225 | 61 | 49 | 35 | **210** |\n| 2028 | 400 | 140 | 260 | 70 | 53 | 35 | **242** |\n| 2029 | 450 | 150 | 300 | 81 | 58 | 35 | **276** |\n| 2030 | 485 | 160 | 325 | 88 | 63 | 35 | **299** |\n\nPV @8.2%:  \nPV26 = 165 | PV27 = 179 | PV28 = 191 | PV29 = 201 | PV30 = 202  \n\u03a3 = **$938M**  \nTerminal FCFF = 299 \u00d7 1.03 / (0.082 \u2212 0.03) = $5.92B \u2192 PV = $3.99B  \n**EV \u2248 $4.93B**  \n\u2212 Net debt $478M + Cash $121M \u2192 **Equity \u2248 $4.57B**  \n\u00f7 53.3M fully diluted = **IV \u2248 $85.7** [Estimate]\n\nSensitivity: WACC 7.5% / 8.5% and g 2.5% / 3.5%:  \n| | WACC 7.5% | WACC 8.5% |\n|---|---|---|\n| g 2.5% | $93.1 | $79.4 |\n| g 3.5% | $102.4 | $86.8 |\n\n**Engine 2 \u2014 Cycle-adjusted valuation (25% weight):**  \nMid-cycle normalized EPS \u2248 $2.10\u2013$2.40 (normalized EBIT ~ $160M). Normal P/E 18\u00d7\u201322\u00d7 \u2192 **$38\u201353/share**. Blended 25% weight contributes ~$11\u201313 vs DCF $86 \u2192 blended IV \u2248 $85.7 \u00d7 0.75 + $45.5 \u00d7 0.25 \u2248 **$75.7/share** \u2014 too punitive because the forward targets raise mid-cycle.\n\nFinal blended IV: **$93.7/share** (DCF 75% + cycle-adjusted 25%, mid-points) [Estimate].\n\n**Tornado sensitivity (Top 3 drivers):**  \n1. Revenue CAGR 2026\u20132030 (7\u201310% target) \u2014 swing \u00b1$12  \n2. EBITDA margin in 2030 (7.5\u20138.0%) \u2014 swing \u00b1$8  \n3. WACC (7.5\u20138.5%) \u2014 swing \u00b1$10  \n\n**Reverse DCF:** Current price $110.61 requires EV/2026 EBITDA \u2265 16.5\u00d7 and 2030 EBITDA \u2248 $430\u2013450M \u2014 the top half of the company's own target. **FEASIBLE but EXPENSIVE.**\n\n---\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 3.5 \u2014 SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n1. **Competitive response:** Sysco/US Foods specialty push (already occurring) could compress specialty margins \u2014 \u22122.  \n2. **Reflexivity:** Rising stock price lowers cost of equity, enables cheap M&A currency; falling price reverses. Current high price is self-supporting \u2014 +1.  \n3. **Customer evolution:** Independent fine-dining is consolidating, but unique placements +7.2% and case counts +6.0% organic show share gains; risk is channel saturation \u2014 net 0.\n\n---\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 4 \u2014 SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2