ng. In a 2022-style simultaneous rates+equity shock, its 1.39 beta and 17.6% short float imply drawdown amplification.\n- Tail correlation: highest with USFD/SYY, restaurant REITs, consumer finance, small-cap value (COVID 2020), and any \"reopening trade.\" Low correlation with staples and utilities. My portfolio-level check: if the book already owns SYY, USFD, or DRI, CHEF adds nothing but correlated tail risk.\n- Conditional VaR (95%, 1-year): model-based estimate \u2248 \u221245% [Assumption \u2014 using 2020 actual \u221260% drawdown as calibration; 40% recovery gap, 17.6% short float]. If the short squeeze runs first (event risk), CVaR could be \u221260% to \u221270% before mean reversion.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 8. MONITORING RULES (THESIS INTEGRITY)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nIf the stock were held or if a future buy is considered, monitoring triggers:\n1. FCF conversion (GAAP FCF / adjusted EBITDA) must reach 35%+ by FY2026, 40%+ by FY2027 \u2014 else thesis KPI #3 fails.\n2. EBITDA margin: quarterly YoY improvement of \u226515bp required; if FY2026 exit margin <6.5%, the 2030 7.5\u20138% path is illusory.\n3. Organic case volume growth: must remain >3% (ex-inflation); <2% for two quarters = demand cycle turning.\n4. Net leverage: must stay \u22642.5x with operating leases included (my adjusted measure); >3.0x = rating/re-assessment event.\n5. 2028 converts: monitor conversion-ratio arithmetic; if the stock stays >$110, full conversion adds ~15% share count and pushes EPS growth to <5% in FY2028.\n6. Macro regime shift: if 10Y Treasury >5.5% or recession probabilities rise, re-cut valuation immediately.\n7. Insider cluster buying/selling over 6 months: no data today [Unconfirmed]; obtain before any entry.\n\nPre-Mortem (\"5 years from now, this position lost money. Why?\"):\n- Scenario A \u2014 \"Priced-for-perfection\": the 2030 plan is executed well but the 18x forward multiple reverts to 10\u201312x, alone causing a \u221230\u201340% total return despite earnings growth.\n- Scenario B \u2014 \"Margin plateau\": adjusted EBITDA margin stalls at 6.8\u20137.0% because food inflation + broadline competition cap it; my 2030 FCFF falls to $170M instead of $262M; IV \u2248 $35.\n- Scenario C \u2014 \"Dilution/leverage trap\": 2028 converts convert at a low premium; interest expense on refinancing at 8%+ plus lease-adjusted leverage of 3x forces equity issuance at low prices.\nEarly warning indicators for all three: FCF conversion <30%; quarterly organic growth <3%; bond spread/refi terms [Unconfirmed \u2014 not available]; adjusted EBITDA margin <6.5% at end of any quarter.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 9. RED TEAM & ADVERSARIAL\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550