550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nT0: 2026-08-24, Price $110.61\nIV (blended): $60; IV (Engine 1): $52.33; Worst-to-best scenario: $32\u201385\nMoS at T0: \u221284% to \u2212111%\nKey assumptions: WACC 10.85%, terminal g 3.5%, EBITDA margin path to 7.4% by 2030, FCF conversion to ~45% by 2030, capex $55\u201365M/yr.\nKey risks to the call: momentum (beat-and-raise) could persist through FY2026, and a short squeeze could drive the stock to $130+ before any fundamental convergence. My 3-year EV under bull = $119, so even the bull case barely clears today's price.\nRed team note: The strongest long argument is that the market has re-rated CHEF as a \"quality compounder\" one to two years early. If the company's FCF conversion hits 40%+ in FY2026 and the macro backdrop improves (Fed cuts), I will revisit with a higher IV and possibly a positive action.\nTrigger to re-evaluate: stock price \u2264 $75 (\u2248 30% below T0) or FCF conversion \u2265 40% (trailing twelve months, ex-SBC).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 12. FINAL EXECUTION OPINION\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nACTION: NO BUY at $110.61. For existing holders: REDUCE / TAKE PROFITS on strength. For investors without a position: WAIT for the price to reach $60\u201375 before beginning a position (that is the 80% CI for intrinsic value and would restore a 15\u201330% margin of safety), or for FCF conversion to exceed 40% for two consecutive quarters (which would trigger a re-valuation upward). Abandon the wait if fundamental evidence (not price) shows the 2030 target path becoming structurally embedded: e.g., FY2026 adjusted EBITDA margin >7.0%, FCF conversion >45%, leverage (incl. leases) <2.0x.\nConviction: LOW. Max weight if re-entry conditions are met: 3\u20135% in a diversified portfolio; one-third initial position with dollar-cost-averaging into any recession-driven drawdown.\nSizing logic: Kelly = 0% at T0; if re-entry at $70 (IV $60\u201385), Kelly \u2248 1\u20133% \u2014 underweight even then, because the base rate of margin expansion is only ~30\u201350% and dilution overhang is unresolved.\nStrategy: (1) Do not chase momentum; (2) If held, use $95 as the mechanical trailing stop; (3) If re-entering at $60\u201375, scale via thirds, pair with a negative-dollar or short-SYY pair trade if available, and commit to the Layer 8 monitoring KPIs on a quarterly basis.\nExecution horizon: 3\u20135 years (not a trading signal).\nFinal verdict: CHEF is a well-run, improving business at a price that already fully discounts the 2030 plan and then some. The short-term momentum is real, but the base rate for a cyclical distributor trading at 18x forward EBITDA ending well is not in your favour. ADJUST: SELL INTO STRENGTH; DO NOT INITIATE; RE-EVALUATE ON FUNDAMENTAL CONFIRMATION.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 END OF REPORT \u2014 RS2 v2.0 ENGINE OUTPUT\n\u25a0 IV: $52\u201360 | MoS: \u22