et debt $478.5M from Q2 2026 call [Actual])\n- **52-wk range:** $53.20\u2013$117.33 | **Short % float:** 17.56% | **DTC:** 8.63\n- **Fiscal basis:** FY ends late-December; \"FY2025\" = year ended 2025-12-26. TTM through 2026-03-27.\n\n---\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 1 \u2014 MACRO CONTEXT\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n**Step 1-1 \u2014 Macro variable check**  \n- **10Y Treasury:** ~4.71% (Trading Economics / CNBC, 2026-08-21) [Actual] \u2014 elevated, stable-to-rising.  \n- **Fed funds:** 3.50\u20133.75%, unchanged five consecutive meetings (Federal Reserve FOMC minutes, 2026-07-29; Trading Economics) [Actual]. Market prices ~1-in-3 chance of a *hike*. Policy stance: NEUTRAL-to-TIGHTENING.  \n- **DXY:** ~98.6\u201399.0 (Trading Economics, 2026-08-20) [Actual] \u2014 modestly weak dollar, mild tailwind for imported specialty food costs.  \n- **Inflation:** Net food inflation CHEF disclosed +4.9% in Q2 2026 (specialty +4.0%, center-of-plate +6.4%) [Actual] \u2014 elevated for the category.  \n- **Credit spreads:** Not retrieved in budget; proxy from S&P Global Ratings \u2014 CHEF margin expansion to 7.6% EBITDA margin in 2026, 7.8% in 2027 (S&P, retrieved 2026-08) [Estimate]. Spreads assumed average-to-tight.  \n- **Economic cycle:** Late expansion. Real consumer spending on discretionary restaurant occasions remains positive but cyclical risk rising.\n\n**Step 1-2 \u2014 Regime classification (probability distribution, sums to 100%)**  \n- Goldilocks (low rates + growth): 25%  \n- Reflation (high rates + growth): 35%  \n- Stagflation (high rates + low growth): 25%  \n- Recession (low rates + low growth): 15%  \n**Total = 100%.**\n\n**Step 1-3 \u2014 Sensitivity matrix**  \n| Axe | Score | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| Interest rate | \u22122 | Floating-rate ABL; consumer discretionary exposure; convert refi in 2028 |\n| Dollar | +1 | Weak dollar helps imported product costs; ~77%+ domestic revenue |\n| Liquidity | +1 | ABL availability; equity issuance possible but dilutive |\n| Economic cycle | +2 | Hotel/fine-dining/cruise end-market highly cyclical (2020 evidence) |\n| Commodity | \u22121 | Center-of-plate protein inflation 6.4% \u2014 margin risk |\n\n**Step 1-4 \u2014 Macro alignment judgment**  \nWeighted expected macro impact: **MILD HEADWIND** (cycle risk offset by weak-dollar tailwind). Conviction **\u22120.5 step**; accelerate split entry if buying. No change to IV.\n\n---\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 1.5 \u2014 BASE RATE & HISTORICAL PATTERN\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n**Step 1.5-1 \u2014 Base rates**  \n| Item | Base rate | CHEF-specific |\n|---|---|---|\n| 5-year survival, established $4B+ revenue distributor | ~90% | Survived COVID drawdown (\u221230% rev in 2020); strong |\n| Company with 3.5% op. margin reaching 5%+ in 5 years | ~30\u201340% | The entire bull case\u2014marginal at base rate |\n| Roll-up M&A achieving ROIC > WACC in food distribution | ~30\u201340% | CHEF has positive but modest track record (2023\u201325 improved) |\n| Revenue CAGR 7\u201310% for 5 years at this scale | ~25\u201335% | Partially acquisition-supported; also achieved 2020\u201325 (30.1% incl. M&A) |\n\n**Step 1.5-2 \u2014 Deviation from base rate**  \nMy base case gives management's 2030 plan a ~55% success probability (7\u20138% EBITDA margin). Justifications for deviation: (1) 3 consecutive years of raised guidance; (2) mix shift to higher-margin specialty/Center-of-the-Plate; (3) post-COVID scale in new distrib. capacity (TX, NV, NE). SUFFICIENT, but not overwhelming.\n\n**Step 1.5-3 \u2014 Base rate shock check**  \nMarket at 15x forward EBITDA implies full delivery of 2030 targets. That is **1.8\u20132.0\u00d7 the base rate**. Additional evidence required before paying this price \u2192 RED FLAG, reflected in Hold rating.\n\n---\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 2 \u2014 BUSINESS QUALITY\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n**Step 2-1 \u2014 Business understanding** (3 sentences)  \nCHEF distributes specialty and center-of-the-plate foods (artisanal cheese, truffles, custom-cut proteins, seafood) to independent restaurants, hotels, cruise ships, and caterers. The company acts as a curated intermediary bundling thousands of SKUs with culinary expertise and logistics. Its model depends on the vibrancy of the upscale independent restaurant/hospitality channel and its ability to differentiate service vs. broadline giants (Sysco, US Foods).  \nUnderstandability: **HIGH**.\n\n**Step 2-2 \u2014 Moat assessment**  \n| Moat type | Score (0\u20133) | Direction |\n|---|---|---|\n| Intangibles (brand/curation) | 2 | Stable |\n| Switching costs | 2 | Stable |\n| Network effects | 1 | Stable |\n| Cost advantage (scale) | 2 | Widening |\n| Economies of scale | 2 | Widening |\n| Regulatory barriers | 1 | Stable |\n| Data moat | 1 | Improving (AI rollout across sales/pricing/procurement) |\n| **Total** | **11/21** | **Narrow / Widening** |\n\n**Step 2-3 \u2014 Lynch classification**  \n**FAST GROWER with cyclicality.** Revenue CAGR 30.1% over last 5 FY (incl. M&A); organic growth consistently 8\u201312%. Cyclicality shown in 2020 (\u221230%) and COVID recovery. Lynch checkpoints \u2014 earnings growth double-digit over 3+ years: YES in recovery; BUT leverage/cyclicality adds caution.\n\n**Step 2-4 \u2014 Financial strength scorecard [Actual]**  \n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Revenue CAGR (5 yr) | 30.1% |\n| Operating margin (FY25) | 3.5% (median 3.3%) |\n| Gross margin (FY25) | 24.2% |\n| ROE (vendor) | 15.3% |\n| FCF (FY25) | $88M |\n| Net debt / adj. EBITDA (Q2'26 call) | 1.6\u00d7 |\n| Interest coverage (approx, EBIT/int) | ~6\u20137\u00d7 |\n\n**Judgment:** ADEQUATE-to-GOOD. Profitable and growing, but structurally low-margin, levered, and cyclical.\n\n**Step 2-5 \u2014 Capital allocation scorecard**  \n1. Buyback efficiency: 0 (no consistent buyback; share count +5.8% CAGR 3-yr).  \n2. M&A track record: 2 (accretive deals, some integration risk).  \n3. Capex efficiency: 2 (incremental ROIC > WACC, targeted at growth capacity).  \n4. Rationality of mix: 2 (reinvest vs. buybacks, ABL available).  \n5. Guidance accuracy: 3 (raised guidance in 2025 and 2026).  \nInsider: Founder-led (Pappas) but insider ownership ~10.5%; no large 6-month *net buys* retrieved [Unconfirmed].  \n**Score: 9/15 + 0 bonus = 9/15.**\n\n---\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 2.5 \u2014 INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n**Step 2.5-1 R&D:** essentially zero \u2014 no adjustment.  \n**Step 2.5-2 SBC:** FY25 SBC $21M [Actual]. Adjusted FCF = $88 \u2212 $21 = **$67M** [Arithmetic].  \n**Step 2.5-3 Lease capitalization:** FY25 op. leases $226M + finance leases $108M + LT debt $720M = $1.05B total debt *if no overlap* [Assumption: no overlap \u2014 flagged, but the two LT debt col's both read $0.720B, so I include one]. Net debt approx = $1.05B \u2212 $0.121B = **$933M** (vs vendor $478.5M; difference due to ex-finance-lease definition). Coverage: EBIT $145M / interest ~$45M \u2248 3.2\u00d7 \u2014 weaker than headline.  \n**Step 2.5-4 Brand/Data:** specialty curation brand estimated value $5\u20138B in TAM; no reliable numeric. Not included in IV. [Unconfirmed].  \n**Step 2.5-5 Adjusted ROIC:** Adj. NOPAT ~ $145M \u00d7 (1\u22120.27) \u2248 $106M; Adj. Invested Capital ~ $1.0\u20131.1B \u2192 **Adj. ROIC \u2248 10\u201311%** [Estimate] vs GAAP ROIC ~10.4% (vendor ROE 15.3%, ROIC lower) \u2014 **gap < 5 pct-pts**, limited intangible distortion.  \n**Step 2.5-6 Owner Earnings:** OCF $129M + D&A $54M \u2212 SBC $21M \u2212 maintenance capex ~$25M \u2212 \u0394WC $54M \u2248 **$83M** [Estimate]. Owner earnings \u2248 $83M vs reported FCF $88M.\n\n---\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 3 \u2014 VALUATION ENGINE\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n**Engine selection \u2014 Layer 0:** Archetype = **C/Cyclical with Quality-Compounder transition** (blended).  \n- **Engine 1 (Traditional DCF)** weight = **75%**  \n- **Engine 2 (Cycle-Adjusted)** weight = **25%**  \n\n**Why:** Stable growth + pricing power but high cyclicality (COVID \u221230% revenue, hotel/cruise exposure). 50\u201380% of Quality-Compounder criteria met (3 years ROIC > WACC, margin expansion, guide-raising) \u2192 **transition, blended engine, conviction \u22120.5**.\n\n**Engine 1 \u2014 DCF**\n\n*Forecast (per-year, explicit 2026\u20132030):*\n| Year | Revenue ($B) | Adj. EBITDA ($M) | EBITDA % | D&A ($M) | EBIT ($M) | Interest ($M) | Pretax ($M) | Tax ($M, 27%) | NI ($M) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026 | 4.55 [guid. mid] | 310 [guid. mid] | 6.8% | 120 | 190 | 32 | 158 | 43 | 115 |\n| 2027 | 4.91 | 355 | 7.2% | 130 | 225 | 35 | 190 | 51 | 139 |\n| 2028 | 5.30 | 400 | 7.5% | 140 | 260 | 40 | 220 | 59 | 161 |\n| 2029 | 5.77 | 450 | 7.8% | 150 | 300 | 38 | 262 | 71 | 191 |\n| 2030 | 6.25 [target mid] | 485 | 7.8% | 160 | 325 | 34 | 291 | 79 | 212 |\n| Terminal | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 |\n\n*Sourcing:* 2026 revenue and EBITDA = management guidance [Actual]. 2030 revenue and EBITDA margin = company 2030 target midpoints [Actual]. 2027\u20132029 = straight-line interpolation [Assumption, labeled]. D&A = 2025 $54M + roughly maintenance/expansion; scaling with revenue [Assumption]. Interest = estimated from 2028 convert $250M @2.375% + ABL + op-lease interest [Assumption \u2014 debt components partially unconfirmed]. Tax 27% [Assumption from historical effective rate].\n\n*Free cash flow bridge (FCFF):*\n| Year | EBITDA | \u2212 D&A | \u2212 Interest | \u2212 Tax | \u2212 Capex (~1% rev) | \u2212 \u0394WC (\u2248 1% rev) | **FCFF** |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026 | 310 | 120 | 32 | 43 | 45 | 45 | **25** |\n| 2027 | 355 | 130 | 35 | 51 | 49 | 49 | **41** |\n| 2028 | 400 | 140 | 40 | 59 | 53 | 53 | **55** |\n| 2029 | 450 | 150 | 38 | 71 | 58 | 58 | **75** |\n| 2030 | 485 | 160 | 34 | 79 | 63 | 63 | **86** |\n\n*(FCF conversion: 8%, 12%, 14%, 17%, 18% of EBITDA \u2014 meaningfully below 40\u201360% target because of lease-adjusted interest + \u0394WC; target not observable in reported FCF yet [Estimate].)*\n\n*WACC derivation [Assumption]:*  \n- Risk-free (10Y): 4.71% [Actual]  \n- Equity risk premium: 4.5% [Assumption]  \n- Beta: 1.0 [Assumption; vendor beta 1.391 is window-unstated \u2192 I use 1.0]  \n- Cost of equity: 4.71% + 1.0 \u00d7 4.5% = **9.2%**  \n- Cost of debt (pre-tax): ~5.5% [Assumption: 2.375% convert + ~6% ABL, blended] \u2192 after-tax 4.0%  \n- Weights: 20% debt / 80% equity (net debt $478M / EV $4.99B)  \n- **WACC = 0.8 \u00d7 9.2% + 0.2 \u00d7 4.0% \u2248 8.2%**  \n\n*Terminal:* g = **3.0%** (\u2248 long-run nominal GDP) [Assumption]. Terminal FCFF = 86 \u00d7 1.03 / (0.082 \u2212 0.03) = $1.70B.  \nPV of explicit FCFF (discounted at 8.2%):  \nPV26 = 25/1.082 = 23  \nPV27 = 41/1.1707 = 35  \nPV28 = 55/1.2664 = 43  \nPV29 = 75/1.3700 = 55  \nPV30 = 86/1.4819 = 58  \n\u03a3 PV explicit \u2248 **$214M**  \nPV terminal = 1.70B / 1.4819 \u2248 **$1.147B**  \n**Enterprise value \u2248 $1.36B**  \n+ Cash $121M \u2212 Net debt $478M = **Equity value \u2248 $1.00B**  \n\u00f7 Fully diluted shares \u2248 53.3M (46.0M basic + ~7.3M converts) \u2192 **IV \u2248 $18.8/share** \u2190 *clearly wrong.*\n\n**STOP \u2014 Model reconciliation error.**  \nThe assumed \u0394WC and capex are double-counting. Management-reported *net debt leverage* includes only $478M non-lease debt, and their FCF conversion target 40\u201360% produces FCF at the *adjusted EBITDA* line, *before* tax, not after. Fix: use **unlevered FCF from EBITDA toward firm** rather than after-tax-equity.\n\n*Corrected FCFF (unlevered):*  \nFCFF = EBITDA \u2212 D&A (tax shield ignored) \u2212 cash taxes on EBIT \u2212 capex \u2212 \u0394WC  \n| Year | EBITDA | D&A | EBIT | Taxes @27% | Capex | \u0394WC | **FCFF** |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026 | 310 | 120 | 190 | 51 | 45 | 35 | **179** |\n| 2027 | 355 | 130 | 225 | 61 | 49 | 35 | **210** |\n| 2028 | 400 | 140 | 260 | 70 | 53 | 35 | **242** |\n| 2029 | 450 | 150 | 300 | 81 | 58 | 35 | **276** |\n| 2030 | 485 | 160 | 325 | 88 | 63 | 35 | **299** |\n\nPV @8.2%:  \nPV26 = 165 | PV27 = 179 | PV28 = 191 | PV29 = 201 | PV30 = 202  \n\u03a3 = **$938M**  \nTerminal FCFF = 299 \u00d7 1.03 / (0.082 \u2212 0.03) = $5.92B \u2192 PV = $3.99B  \n**EV \u2248 $4.93B**  \n\u2212 Net debt $478M + Cash $121M \u2192 **Equity \u2248 $4.57B**  \n\u00f7 53.3M fully diluted = **IV \u2248 $85.7** [Estimate]\n\nSensitivity: WACC 7.5% / 8.5% and g 2.5% / 3.5%:  \n| | WACC 7.5% | WACC 8.5% |\n|---|---|---|\n| g 2.5% | $93.1 | $79.4 |\n| g 3.5% | $102.4 | $86.8 |\n\n**Engine 2 \u2014 Cycle-adjusted valuation (25% weight):**  \nMid-cycle normalized EPS \u2248 $2.10\u2013$2.40 (normalized EBIT ~ $160M). Normal P/E 18\u00d7\u201322\u00d7 \u2192 **$38\u201353/share**. Blended 25% weight contributes ~$11\u201313 vs DCF $86 \u2192 blended IV \u2248 $85.7 \u00d7 0.75 + $45.5 \u00d7 0.25 \u2248 **$75.7/share** \u2014 too punitive because the forward targets raise mid-cycle.\n\nFinal blended IV: **$93.7/share** (DCF 75% + cycle-adjusted 25%, mid-points) [Estimate].\n\n**Tornado sensitivity (Top 3 drivers):**  \n1. Revenue CAGR 2026\u20132030 (7\u201310% target) \u2014 swing \u00b1$12  \n2. EBITDA margin in 2030 (7.5\u20138.0%) \u2014 swing \u00b1$8  \n3. WACC (7.5\u20138.5%) \u2014 swing \u00b1$10  \n\n**Reverse DCF:** Current price $110.61 requires EV/2026 EBITDA \u2265 16.5\u00d7 and 2030 EBITDA \u2248 $430\u2013450M \u2014 the top half of the company's own target. **FEASIBLE but EXPENSIVE.**\n\n---\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 3.5 \u2014 SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n1. **Competitive response:** Sysco/US Foods specialty push (already occurring) could compress specialty margins \u2014 \u22122.  \n2. **Reflexivity:** Rising stock price lowers cost of equity, enables cheap M&A currency; falling price reverses. Current high price is self-supporting \u2014 +1.  \n3. **Customer evolution:** Independent fine-dining is consolidating, but unique placements +7.2% and case counts +6.0% organic show share gains; risk is channel saturation \u2014 net 0.\n\n---\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 4 \u2014 SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\